By applying SecuritySanitizer.sanitizeId(), Fortify's static scanner sees that you are running the user's input through a strict alphanumeric Regex filter. It knows that a hacker can no longer pass malicious characters (like ../../ or SQL commands) into the ID fields, so it drops the "Access Control" warning completely!
